==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[enrol]] {{i|UK}} {{i|CA}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-enroll.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{transitive}} To [[enter]] (a name) in a [[register]], [[roll]] or [[list]]
# {{transitive}} To [[enlist]] (someone) or make (someone) a [[member]] of
#: ''They were eager to '''enroll''' new recruits.''
# {{intransitive}} To [[enlist]] oneself (in something) or become a [[member]] (of something)
#: ''Have you '''enrolled''' in classes yet for this term?''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|enter in a register}} [[list]], [[note]], [[note down]], [[record]], [[register]]
* {{sense|enlist}} [[enlist]], [[sign up]], [[subscribe]]
* {{sense|become a member}} [[enlist]], [[join]], [[join up]], [[sign up]], [[subscribe]]
* {{sense|join a class}} [[add]], [[register]] for {{qualifier|synonyms for “enroll in [a class]”}}

====Derived terms====
* [[enrollee]]
* [[enroller]]
* [[enrollment]]

